doc: StatColorWords is a Continuous static's ChangeColorWordsTo$ ChosenColor over Affected$ Spell,Permanent in AffectedZone$ Stack,Battlefield (Swirl the Mists; CR 612.5): every colour word in the text of the spells on the stack and the permanents on the battlefield becomes the source's recorded colour word. The kernel holds no per-object text (kop.ExtChangeText), so it rewrites the colour words where the faces are read (static_colorwords.go): a target spec's filter colour masks and a printed Protection keyword's colours of an affected spell or permanent read as gorge's rewritten face reads them (every colour word of the face replaced by the last-live source's colour; a source with no recorded colour changes nothing, as gorge's colourWordEffects fails closed), and an ability on the stack keeps the colour it was put on the stack under (its text is frozen then). A face whose rewritten word also sits on a surface the model does not read (CardDef.CWUnmodelled: the type line, the SVars, any other ability, trigger, static or replacement parameter) stalls the game (StallTextChange, unmodelled) at pushBuild and before each priority grant, behind prep.anyColorWords.
